{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3077","id":4562187512,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD-10-A","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3077","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3077.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3077.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3077","number":3077,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Retry the hermetic fetch so one network blip cannot discard a 270-node run","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Retry the hermetic fetch so one network blip cannot discard a 270-node run\n\n[hermit2, review-3069, claude-opus-5, devbig014, role=impl]\n\nPlain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nThe fetch phase is a validate run's ONLY network phase -- everything after it\nbuilds offline from what it fetched -- so every node depends on it. One transient\nfailure there therefore discards the whole run. Measured on run 1843: the node\nfailed in 4.86 seconds and the run ended 30 passed, 1 failed, 239 skipped against\na 270-node plan. Roughly 25 minutes of machine time produced no coverage at all.\n\nThe failure was `curl [60] SSL peer certificate ... unable to get local issuer\ncertificate` on a single crates.io CDN download, in a run whose DNS resolved,\nwhose network negative-control passed, and whose two git remotes both succeeded.\nIt is transient, established three ways: the identical `cargo fetch --locked`\nreproduces successfully with a fresh CARGO_HOME, curl to the same host returns\n200 through the proxy, and run 1842 passed this same node in 95 seconds. Cargo\nwill not retry it itself, because cargo retries only what it classifies as\nSPURIOUS and a certificate-verification failure is not in that set.\n\nTask: add-bounded-retry-so-one-network-blip-cannot-discard-a-270-node-validate\n\nWHAT THIS ADDS. A bounded retry around the fetch phase's network operations:\n3 attempts including the first, linear 5-second backoff, and a 300-second\ndeadline after which no new attempt starts.\n\n⚠️ APPLIED TO ALL THREE NETWORK OPERATIONS, not only the one observed failing.\nThe phase runs cargo fetch for each workspace manifest AND\nprepare-rust-scripts.sh --fetch-only. Repairing only the arm where a defect was\nseen leaves it wherever it was not seen; that exact mistake was made in a\nsibling change earlier today and is why the retry is one shared function rather\nthan three call sites.\n\n⚠️ THE RETRY MUST NOT MASK A PERSISTENT FAILURE, which shaped three decisions:\n  * The child's streams are INHERITED, never captured, so the failing command's\n    own words reach the run log exactly as before.\n  * The final failure returns the CHILD's exit status, not a synthetic one, so\n    exit 101 still reaches the ledger as exit 101.\n  * The deadline exists so a retry can never convert a diagnosable exit into a\n    TIMEOUT KILL, which would hide the cause completely -- strictly worse than\n    the failure being survived.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately, and both were explicit prohibitions. TLS verification is\nuntouched: a retry turns a visible transient into a second attempt, while\nrelaxing verification would turn it into a silent supply-chain hole. And no\ntimeout is raised: the node dies in ~5 seconds against a 600-second budget, so a\ntimeout was never the constraint.\n\nDeterminism\n\nNo guest behaviour is involved; this is host-side fetch orchestration. The retry\nis a pure control-flow bound with no clock dependence beyond a fixed backoff, and\n`cargo fetch --locked` remains the operation -- every byte still checked against\nthe selected Cargo.lock, exact versions and content checksums for registry\ncrates, exact revisions for git dependencies. A retried fetch produces the same\nverified bytes or fails.\n\nLinux Semantics\n\nNo guest syscall, process, signal or exit-status behaviour is affected.\n\nValidation\n\nci/hermetic/tests/test-retry-fetch.sh, 14 checks, proving it BOTH WAYS because a\nretry proven only on the happy path is not proven:\n  * a transient failure is survived, really retries, and the first attempt's own\n    error still reaches the log;\n  * a persistent failure STILL FAILS, bounded at exactly 3 attempts, returning\n    the command's own exit 101, with curl's error surfaced and the final line\n    saying the cause is above rather than claiming to be it;\n  * an exhausted deadline stops early, still returning the real status and cause;\n  * control: a succeeding command runs exactly once with no retry chatter.\n\nThe test SOURCES the real helper rather than reimplementing it, and is wired into\n`make lint-checks` -- a test nothing runs is the defect this project keeps\nfinding. Control: reintroducing the swallowed-status bug fails 7 of the 14 checks\nand the script exits 1, so the gate bites.\n\n⚠️ THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS HELPER HAD A REAL BUG AND THE TEST CAUGHT IT. It\nused `if \"$@\"; then ... fi; rc=$?`, but after an if statement completes `$?` is\nthe status OF THE IF, which is 0 when the condition was false -- silently turning\nevery failure into success. The fix and the reason are recorded in the file.\n\nshellcheck over the 205 tracked shell files is unchanged at 99 pre-existing\nfindings, with zero in the new files.\n\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T19:24:34Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T19:24:34Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8b6708fdda8f86c45375e0cdbcbcdc044feaa94c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3077/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3077/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3077/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/552c68b8f763e4fc431928b44e637b61d5d5d83a","head":{"label":"rrnewton:review-3069/bounded-fetch-retry","ref":"review-3069/bounded-fetch-retry","sha":"552c68b8f763e4fc431928b44e637b61d5d5d83a","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":5636